STEP 7 — Tailwind CSS (v4)

What I did:
- Installed Tailwind CSS v4 and its official Vite plugin:
    tailwindcss          4.3.3
    @tailwindcss/vite    4.3.3
- Wired the plugin into frontend/vite.config.js:
    import tailwindcss from '@tailwindcss/vite'
    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()]
- Enabled Tailwind in the CSS by adding this line at the top of
  frontend/src/index.css:
    @import "tailwindcss";

Why the v4 approach:
- Tailwind v4 is the current standard and the simplest setup. It does NOT
  need a tailwind.config.js or a postcss.config.js file. The Vite plugin
  plus the single @import line is all that's required. You can use Tailwind
  utility classes in your components right away.
